Data licenses
=============

The lists in this branch are generated daily from third-party data. They are
not covered by the MIT license of the build code. Each list keeps the license
of the source it was built from. A preset that combines several sources is
distributed under the most restrictive license among them; CC BY-SA 4.0 is
one-way compatible with GPL-3.0, so a mix of the two is GPL-3.0. The full
text of GPL-3.0 is in COPYING.GPL-3.0 next to this file.

Sources
-------

1. v2fly/domain-list-community, MIT License
   https://github.com/v2fly/domain-list-community
   Used for: geosite/<name>.txt, except the runetfreedom categories in 2.

2. runetfreedom/russia-blocked-geosite, GPL-3.0
   https://github.com/runetfreedom/russia-blocked-geosite
   Used for: geosite/ru-blocked, ru-blocked-all, ru-available-only-inside,
   refilter, antifilter-download, antifilter-download-community, gfw,
   win-spy, win-update, win-extra, u17.
   Its data comes from antifilter.download, community.antifilter.download
   and re:filter (https://github.com/1andrevich/Re-filter-lists, MIT).

3. runetfreedom/russia-blocked-geoip, GPL-3.0
   https://github.com/runetfreedom/russia-blocked-geoip
   Used for: geoip/ and geoip6/ ru-blocked, ru-blocked-community,
   ru-whitelist, re-filter, ddos-guard, yandex.
   Its data comes from the same projects as 2.

4. Loyalsoldier/geoip, CC BY-SA 4.0
   https://github.com/Loyalsoldier/geoip
   Used for: all other geoip/ and geoip6/ lists (countries and services).
   Country data is based on MaxMind GeoLite2:

   This product includes GeoLite Data created by MaxMind, available from
   https://www.maxmind.com

   GeoLite data is provided under the GeoLite End User License Agreement
   (https://www.maxmind.com/en/geolite2/eula), which incorporates CC BY-SA 4.0.
   The agreement requires using the current version of the data and deleting
   older copies within 30 days of a new release. Keep a copy of these lists
   up to date, or do not keep it.

